					</div>
					<div class="essay-body">
						<h3>Who is Maa Adya Mahakali?</h3>
						<p>
							<strong>Maa Adya Mahakali</strong> is revered as the primordial source: the first, original power from
							which creation unfolds. In this form she is linked with time, change, and the full cycle of arising,
							sustaining, and dissolving.
						</p>
						<p>
							As Mahakali, she stands beyond ordinary limits and is remembered as the force that cuts through
							ignorance, ego, and fear. For devotees, that makes her both fierce and intimate: a presence approached
							for truth, courage, and surrender.
						</p>
						<h3>Why People Chant</h3>
						<p>
							For many devotees, the Sahasranama is recited as prayer, remembrance, and steady practice. The names
							are a way of drawing closer to Maa Adya and returning the mind to devotion.
						</p>
